            </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
        </geography>
        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>While Open End yarn production; electricity, heat energy are consumed and raw material wastes occurs. Electricity and heat energy consumption were calculated according to yarn count for whole Open End production process. The consumptions of energy according to yarn counts were moddeled according to Ring Spinning wich is similar technology for yarn spinning. This data covers all the fiber production, yarn production and yarn fixing steps.

A user employing this service within their models should use it along with an 1.12 kg of material to produce an 1 kg of yarn. 0.12 kg of waste shall also be added. A user is responsible for defining the nature of the recycling and/or disposal of this waste. Additionally, a user is responsible for accounting transportation expenditures for all extra input and output materials that need to be modelled alongside this service.*

*Ref: Altun, S. (2012). Prediction of textile waste profile and recycling opportunities in Turk. Fibres &amp; Textiles in Eastern Europe.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
            <technologicalApplicability>na</technologicalApplicability>
